WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.921
Celia Cruz left Cuba on tour in 1960 and never went back.

2
00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:08.878
In exile she became the Queen of Salsa, carried Afro-Cuban music around

3
00:00:08.878 --> 00:00:12.434
the world, and received the National Medal of Arts from the President.

4
00:00:12.784 --> 00:00:18.589
She was born in Havana on 21 October 1925, into a poor family.

5
00:00:18.939 --> 00:00:20.953
According to her biographers, Castro's

6
00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:23.339
government barred her from returning to Cuba.

7
00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:26.051
She made her life in New York and New Jersey,

8
00:00:26.051 --> 00:00:28.519
and sang about Cuba for the rest of her career.

9
00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:32.651
In 1997, at a ceremony marking fifty years of her

10
00:00:32.651 --> 00:00:36.588
musical career, she gave a stage costume, shoes and

11
00:00:36.588 --> 00:00:41.373
all, to the Smithsonian's National Museum of American History.

12
00:00:41.723 --> 00:00:44.387
In 2024 the United States Mint put her on a

13
00:00:44.387 --> 00:00:47.795
